[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two shallow, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged oak wood table with visible grain and small nicks. The composition is a 3/4 overhead angle, ensuring every component of the Spanish-style skillet meal is clearly visible. The bowls are filled with a hearty mixture of tomato-based sauce, creamy butter beans, and fluffy quinoa, with wilted baby spinach leaves interspersed throughout. Four eggs are nestled into the mixture, their whites cooked to a firm opaque white with soft, runny, golden-orange yolks visible. Dollops of thick Greek yogurt are placed strategically around the edges of the skillet mixture, creating a creamy contrast against the deep red tomato sauce. The dish is garnished with a fresh, irregular scatter of chopped bright green parsley. Shallow depth of field keeps the foreground bowl sharp while the second bowl and a wooden spoon resting on the table are softly blurred. Soft natural light flows from a window on the left, casting gentle, natural shadows and creating a subtle sheen on the oil-kissed sauce. The atmosphere is warm, cozy, and lived-in, with a few stray grains of quinoa and a small splash of red sauce on the wooden surface near the bowls. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no artificial lighting. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. Indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces."
  }
]
